title: Proposition 28
---
order: 28
---
short_label: VI.28
---
red_highlight: yes
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To apply a parallelogram equal to a given rectilinear figure to a given straight line but falling short by a parallelogram similar to a given one; thus the given rectilinear figure must not be greater than the parallelogram described on the half of the straight line and similar to the given parallelogram.
----
proof:

[!just VI.27]

Let {C|Ct} be the given rectilinear figure, {AB} the given straight line,  and {D|Dt} the given parallelogram, and let {C|Ct} not be greater than the parallelogram described on the half of {AB} similar to the given parallelogram {D|Dt}.

It is required to apply a parallelogram equal to the given rectilinear figure {C|Ct} to the given straight line {AB} but falling short by a parallelogram similar to {D|Dt}.

